From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: homescoop <homescoop@ai-ecoverse.invalid>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 10:35:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wasi: a WASI platform for interpreters and wheels

wasix-python reports sysconfig.get_platform() 'wasi-0.0.0-wasm32'.
get_interpreter_info.py passes it on like the BSDs, and uv gets an
Os::Wasi { release } with the wheel platform tag wasi_0_0_0_wasm32
(what pip and packaging compute for the same interpreter). PyPI has no
such wheels, so pure-Python wheels and sdists install; compiled packages
come from homescoop's py-* packages.
---
 .../src/minimum_libc_version.rs               |  1 +
 crates/uv-platform-tags/src/platform.rs       |  5 +++++
 crates/uv-platform-tags/src/platform_tag.rs   | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 crates/uv-platform-tags/src/tags.rs           | 12 ++++++++++++
 crates/uv-platform/src/os.rs                  |  1 +
 .../python/get_interpreter_info.py            |  1 +
 crates/uv-torch/src/backend.rs                |  3 +++
 7 files changed, 42 insertions(+)

